# L §3.3 accrue: "Exact where the power is an integer; otherwise it needs to u": effective over 181/365 of a year.
# The power comes from the rows (the dates), so the check is the run's, made where the value is read, in load's words:
# RUN-DOMAIN (L §8.4 Load refuses what load sees; tally 2.1.8 §4, #162). 2.1.7's refcore printed LOAD-TO at run.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input p: money PLN
input r: rate
input d1: date
input d2: date
def a: num PLN = accrue(p, r, d1, d2, act365, effective) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  p = 1 000.00 PLN
  r = 12 %/year
  d1 = 2026-01-01
  d2 = 2026-07-01

ask q: a law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-DOMAIN accrue needs to u
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
